The diagram shows a sector. Explain the difference between its arc length and its perimeter.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(2.5,0) node[midway,below] {$r$};
\draw (0,0)--(70:2.5) node[midway,above left] {$r$};
\draw (2.5,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=70,radius=2.5];
\path (35:2.9) node {$l$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

Calculate the arc length of this sector. Give an exact answer in terms of $\pi$, then round to two decimal places.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(2.5,0) node[midway,below] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\draw (0,0)--(75:2.5);
\draw (2.5,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=75,radius=2.5];
\draw (0.6,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=75,radius=0.6];
\path (37.5:1.05) node {$75^\circ$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

The marked angle is the exterior angle of this sector. Calculate the arc length to two decimal places.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(2.5,0) node[midway,below] {$9\text{ m}$};
\draw (0,0)--(140:2.5);
\draw (140:2.5) arc[start angle=140,end angle=360,radius=2.5];
\draw (0.6,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=140,radius=0.6];
\path (70:1.05) node {$140^\circ$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

Calculate the perimeter of this sector. Give an exact answer in terms of $\pi$, then round to one decimal place.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(2.5,0) node[midway,below] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw (0,0)--(144:2.5);
\draw (2.5,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=144,radius=2.5];
\draw (0.6,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=144,radius=0.6];
\path (72:1.05) node {$144^\circ$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

Calculate the perimeter of this quadrant to one decimal place.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(2.5,0) node[midway,below] {$8\text{ m}$};
\draw (0,0)--(0,2.5);
\draw (2.5,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=90,radius=2.5];
\draw (0.25,0)--(0.25,0.25)--(0,0.25);
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

A student says, “The perimeter of this semicircle is half the circumference.” Explain the mistake and calculate the correct perimeter to one decimal place.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-2.5,0)--(2.5,0);
\draw (2.5,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=2.5];
\draw[<->] (-2.5,-0.45)--(2.5,-0.45) node[midway,below] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

A sector is five eighths of a whole circle of radius $8\text{ cm}$. Calculate its perimeter to the nearest centimetre.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(2.3,0) node[midway,below] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\draw (0,0)--(225:2.3);
\draw (2.3,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=225,radius=2.3];
\path (112.5:1.1) node {$\frac58\text{ of a circle}$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
